# word_shift_carry:
# The word of width w whose least significant bit is c and whose bits above
# are the w - 1 low bits of x: x shifted up by one, c shifted in, the top
# bit dropped. Each bit of x is read once.
. (λtuple. tuple λw. nat_fold (λc x. word_end) (λrest c x. x λa above. word_cell c λ. rest a above) w)
λ word_shift_carry
# word_shift:
# x doubled, wrapped to w bits: x shifted up by one with false shifted in.
. (λtuple. tuple λw. word_shift_carry w false)
λ word_shift
# word_multiply:
# The product of two words of width w, wrapped to w bits: at the least
# significant bit b of y and the bits y' above it, x y = (b ? x : 0) + 2 (x y'),
# every sum and every doubling wrapped to w bits. The recursion is on the
# bits of y left, w of them, and each intermediate word is read once, since
# a reading that does not share computes a word read twice twice. The
# reference's steps at the widths 4, 8, 16 and 32 (2026-10-31, the operands
# -2147481450 and -2147483603 masked to the width): 4,469, 16,651, 65,867
# and 260,801, about four times for each doubling of the width.
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ w
    . nat_fold
      (λx y. word_zero w)
      (λrest x y. y λb y_above. word_add w (b x λ. word_zero w) λ. word_shift w λ. rest x y_above) w
  )
λ word_multiply
. export word_shift_carry word_shift word_multiply
